<body>

  <header class="animate">
    <h1 class="poster-title">Large Language Models in Medicine: Opportunities, Risks, and the Path Forward</h1>
    <div class="poster-subtitle">A comprehensive review of how large language models are transforming clinical practice, medical research, and healthcare delivery — along with the critical challenges that must be addressed.</div>
  </header>

  <div class="metrics animate delay-1">
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-value">>90%</div>
      <div class="metric-label">GPT-4 USMLE Score</div>
      <div class="metric-desc">Exceeded the passing threshold on all three steps of the United States Medical Licensing Examination.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-value">500+</div>
      <div class="metric-label">PubMed Articles (2023)</div>
      <div class="metric-desc">Over 500 peer-reviewed publications on LLMs in medicine published in 2023 alone.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card risk">
      <div class="metric-value">Up to 30%</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Hallucination Rate</div>
      <div class="metric-desc">Models can generate fabricated references or inaccurate clinical information in up to 30% of outputs.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-value">$10.5B</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Global LLM Health Market</div>
      <div class="metric-desc">The healthcare LLM market is projected to reach $10.5 billion globally by the year 2030.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="poster-content">

    <!-- LEFT COLUMN -->
    <div class="column animate delay-2">
      <section>
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2 class="section-title">What Are LLMs and Why Do They Matter for Medicine?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-text">
          <p>Large language models (LLMs) such as <strong>GPT-4</strong>, <strong>Med-PaLM 2</strong>, and <strong>LLaMA</strong> are foundation models trained on vast corpora of text data. Their rapid emergence has reshaped clinical practice, biomedical research, and medical education.</p>
          <p>As demonstrated in a landmark July 2023 <em>Nature Medicine</em> review, these models exhibit remarkable capabilities in understanding and generating medical text, transitioning rapidly from benchmark successes to real-world pilot deployments.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section style="flex: 1;">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2 class="section-title">Key Clinical and Research Applications</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="app-list">
          <div class="app-item">
            <span class="app-badge">Pilot deployments</span>
            <div class="app-title">Clinical Documentation</div>
            <div class="app-desc">Automated note generation and discharge summaries, reducing administrative burden.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="app-item">
            <span class="app-badge">Early adoption</span>
            <div class="app-title">Patient Communication</div>
            <div class="app-desc">Answering patient questions and simplifying complex medical jargon into plain language.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="app-item">
            <span class="app-badge">Active use</span>
            <div class="app-title">Medical Education</div>
            <div class="app-desc">Exam preparation, case-based learning, and interactive tutoring for medical students.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="app-item">
            <span class="app-badge">Research stage</span>
            <div class="app-title">Diagnostic Support</div>
            <div class="app-desc">Differential diagnosis generation and nuanced radiology report interpretation.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- RIGHT COLUMN -->
    <div class="column animate delay-3">

      <section>
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2 class="section-title">Performance Benchmarks and Evidence</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-text">
          <p>LLM performance on standardized medical examinations serves as a key proxy for medical knowledge encoding, though performance on real-world clinical scenarios remains an active area of investigation.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="chart-wrapper">
          <div role="img" aria-label="Bar chart showing LLM performance on medical benchmarks compared to passing thresholds">
            <div class="chart-container">
              <canvas id="performanceChart"></canvas>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="risk-section" style="flex: 1;">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2 class="section-title">Risks, Limitations, and Ethical Concerns</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-list">
          <div class="risk-item">
            <div class="risk-num">1</div>
            <div class="risk-text"><strong>Hallucinations & Accuracy</strong> LLMs can fabricate plausible-sounding but incorrect medical information or fake citations.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="risk-item">
            <div class="risk-num">2</div>
            <div class="risk-text"><strong>Bias and Equity</strong> Models may perpetuate or amplify biases present in training data, leading to disparities in care recommendations.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="risk-item">
            <div class="risk-num">3</div>
            <div class="risk-text"><strong>Privacy & Security</strong> Patient data used in prompts may be transmitted to external servers, raising HIPAA and GDPR compliance concerns.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="risk-item">
            <div class="risk-num">4</div>
            <div class="risk-text"><strong>Automation Bias</strong> The risk of over-reliance, where clinicians accept LLM outputs without sufficient critical appraisal or oversight.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- FOOTER FRAMEWORK -->
  <section class="framework-section animate delay-4">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 class="section-title">A Framework for Responsible Deployment</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="framework-grid">
      <div class="fw-step">
        <div class="fw-icon">🔬</div>
        <div class="fw-title">Rigorous Evaluation</div>
        <div class="fw-desc">Prospective evaluation in diverse clinical settings before live deployment.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fw-step">
        <div class="fw-icon">👨‍⚕️</div>
        <div class="fw-title">Human-in-the-Loop</div>
        <div class="fw-desc">Ensuring clinician oversight and review of all LLM-generated outputs.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fw-step">
        <div class="fw-icon">📊</div>
        <div class="fw-title">Transparent Reporting</div>
        <div class="fw-desc">Clear communication of model limitations, data sources, and failure modes.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fw-step">
        <div class="fw-icon">⚖️</div>
        <div class="fw-title">Equity Audits</div>
        <div class="fw-desc">Continuous assessment of differential performance across patient populations.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fw-step">
        <div class="fw-icon">📋</div>
        <div class="fw-title">Regulatory Alignment</div>
        <div class="fw-desc">Adherence to evolving FDA, EMA, and WHO guidance on AI medical devices.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    Chart.defaults.animation = false;

    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
      // Safe initialization for the chart
      if (typeof Chart === 'undefined') return;

      var ctx = document.getElementById('performanceChart');
      if (!ctx) return;

      new Chart(ctx, {
        type: 'bar',
        data: {
          labels: ['GPT-4 (USMLE)', 'Med-PaLM 2 (MedQA)', 'GPT-3.5 (USMLE)', 'Human Passing Threshold'],
          datasets: [{
            label: 'Benchmark Score (%)',
            data: [92, 86.5, 60, 60],
            backgroundColor: [
              '#0F3A64', // Accent (GPT-4)
              '#3B82F6', // Accent-secondary (Med-PaLM 2)
              '#94A3B8', // Gray (GPT-3.5)
              '#E2E8F0'  // Light Gray (Threshold)
            ],
            borderRadius: 8,
            borderWidth: 0,
            barThickness: 60
          }]
        },
        options: {
          responsive: true,
          maintainAspectRatio: false,
          plugins: {
            legend: { display: false },
            tooltip: {
              enabled: true,
              titleFont: { size: 24, family: 'Inter' },
              bodyFont: { size: 28, family: 'Inter', weight: 'bold' },
              padding: 20,
              cornerRadius: 12,
              displayColors: false
            }
          },
          scales: {
            y: {
              beginAtZero: true,
              max: 100,
              ticks: { 
                font: { size: 24, family: 'Inter', weight: '600' },
                color: '#475569',
                callback: function(value) { return value + '%'; },
                padding: 16
              },
              grid: { color: '#E2E8F0', drawBorder: false }
            },
            x: {
              ticks: { 
                font: { size: 24, family: 'Inter', weight: '600' },
                color: '#0F172A',
                padding: 16
              },
              grid: { display: false, drawBorder: false }
            }
          },
          layout: { padding: { top: 30, right: 30, bottom: 0, left: 0 } }
        }
      });

      // Horizontal reference line for passing threshold (approx 60%)
      const plugin = {
        id: 'horizontalLine',
        beforeDraw: function(chart) {
          const ctx = chart.ctx;
          const yAxis = chart.scales.y;
          const xAxis = chart.scales.x;
          const yPos = yAxis.getPixelForValue(60);

          ctx.save();
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.moveTo(xAxis.left, yPos);
          ctx.lineTo(xAxis.right, yPos);
          ctx.lineWidth = 4;
          ctx.strokeStyle = '#E11D48'; // Negative/Coral
          ctx.setLineDash([10, 10]);
          ctx.stroke();
          ctx.restore();

          ctx.fillStyle = '#E11D48';
          ctx.font = 'bold 24px Inter';
          ctx.fillText('Passing Threshold (~60%)', xAxis.left + 20, yPos - 15);
        }
      };

      Chart.register(plugin);
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
EOF

